A||||3||yellowfiero||ignition timing help||||9||
Z||000000||yellowfiero||08-06-2000||01:36 PM||||At what degree should the ignition timing be set on a -87 V6? I have a Crane Compucam and an ADS Superchip installed, does that affect the timing setting?<BR> / Henrik||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT Bastard||08-06-2000||01:51 PM||||10 degrees is stock, so I'd start there.  Just advance it a couple degrees at a time and test it out.  Are you jumpering the terminals when you time it?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||yellowfiero||08-07-2000||11:33 AM||||OK thanks! Jump the terminals....? Ehh, well I don't know what that is in swedish. I found out that it seems to run well somewhere around 13-20. Lower than that it hesitates on quick acceleration.... I'll keep on testing... :-) ||||reg||10
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-07-2000||06:10 PM||||to get max out of a modified engine usually OEM specs no longer work. For timing i advance it to point where it starts knocking/detonating. then retard it a couple degrees at a time till that stops, then retard a couple more degrees and tighten dist. then for final test, see if engine still cranks over normally hot. If it doesnt crank evenly retard it more till it will crank normally. Make a note of what the setting is so you wont have to start over next time.||||reg||1
